ally, though, Hardy remained cloaked in the arms of this very upper class during the publication of these books, acting at all times in complete convention with the rules of society. Was he using his books to express himself in a way he felt unable to do in the company he kept, or did he know sensationalism would sell? Award-winning author Claire Tomalin expertly reconstructs the life that led Hardy to maintain conventionality and write revolution.Born in Dorset in 1840, Hardy came of age in rather meager circumstances. At sixteen, he left home for London and slowly worked his way through many rejections to become a published writer.","pageCount":512,"publicationYear":2006,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"English Authors","sourceId":"source-open-library-thomas-hardy-the-time-torn-man-claire-tomalin"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Nonfiction","sourceId":"source-open-library-thomas-hardy-the-time-torn-man-claire-tomalin"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography & Autobiography","sourceId":"source-open-library-thomas-hardy-the-time-torn-man-claire-tomalin"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Authors, English","sourceId":"source-open-library-thomas-hardy-the-time-torn-man-claire-tomalin"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-thomas-hardy-the-time-torn-man-claire-tomalin"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Hardy, thomas, 1840-1928","sourceId":"source-open-library-thomas-hardy-the-time-torn-man-claire-tomalin"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Authors, biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-thomas-hardy-the-time-torn-man-claire-tomalin"}],"displaySummary":"When he published Tess of the d'Urbervilles and Jude the Obscure late in his career, Hardy explored a very different world th